**Allegro ETRM — Contract #PPA-2022-008**
Counterparty: Apex Solar Partners — Cimarron 2 LLC | Product: Solar + Storage (80 MW / 40 MWh) | Contracted COD: December 31, 2025 | Sunset Clause: 'If COD is not achieved within 18 months of Target COD, either party may terminate without penalty.' | Status: Pre-COD

**SharePoint — /Governance/Delegation_of_Authority_Matrix_v3.pdf (Published Jan 2025)**
Contract Modifications — Energy Supply Agreements:
- Amendments < $500K impact: Director, Energy Supply
- Amendments $500K-$2M impact: VP, Energy Supply
- Amendments > $2M impact: SVP + CFO co-signature
- Extension of contractual deadlines: VP, Energy Supply (regardless of dollar impact)
Note: 'Email approvals acceptable for time-sensitive matters; must be followed by wet signature within 30 days.'

**Outlook — From: j.castillo@apexsolarpartners.com (Aug 8, 2025)**
To: marcus.trujillo@conduitenergy.com
CC: sarah.lindqvist@conduitenergy.com, legal-energy@conduitenergy.com
Subject: Cimarron 2 — COD Extension Request

'Marcus — as discussed, supply chain delays on the BESS modules are pushing our ICD back to Q2 2026. We're requesting a 9-month extension of the Target COD to September 30, 2026. All other terms unchanged. Attached: updated construction schedule and module delivery confirmation from CATL.'

**Outlook — From: marcus.trujillo@conduitenergy.com (Aug 12, 2025)**
To: j.castillo@apexsolarpartners.com
CC: sarah.lindqvist@conduitenergy.com
Subject: RE: Cimarron 2 — COD Extension Request

'Jorge — understood on the BESS delays. 9-month extension to Sep 30, 2026 is acceptable. Consider this our consent. Sarah will update the tracking. Let's get the formal amendment papered in the next few weeks.'

**SharePoint — /Renewables/PPAs/Cimarron2/Amendments/**
Folder is empty. No executed amendment on file.

**Teams — DM between Sarah Lindqvist and Amy Vasquez (Legal) (Oct 14, 2025)**
@sarah.lindqvist: Hey Amy — the Cimarron 2 COD extension that Marcus approved back in August, did that ever get papered?
@amy.vasquez: I don't have it in my queue. Was it sent to me?
@sarah.lindqvist: I thought so but let me check. Marcus approved via email. The delegation matrix says VP approval is fine for deadline extensions.
@amy.vasquez: Wait — Marcus is Director level, not VP. Dave Morton is the VP.
@sarah.lindqvist: ... oh.
@amy.vasquez: Yeah. I'd get Dave to ratify it ASAP. If the developer tries to hold us to the extension and it's challenged, an unauthorized approval is voidable.
@sarah.lindqvist: But Marcus's email said 'consider this our consent.' And it's been two months.
@amy.vasquez: Estoppel argument maybe, but messy. Just get Dave to sign. Don't put this in writing anywhere else.
[No further messages]

**SAP — Project Tracker (Custom Z-table)**
Project: Cimarron 2 | Status: Pre-COD | Target COD: 12/31/2025 | Extension: None recorded | Milestone payments: None released post-Aug 2025.

**Teams — #energy-supply (Jan 6, 2026, 8:02 AM)**
@dave.morton: Happy new year team. Quick audit — how many projects missed their 2025 COD targets?
@sarah.lindqvist: Three. Cimarron 2, Platte River 7, and Greenfield South.
@dave.morton: Cimarron 2 has a sunset clause right? Are we at risk?
@sarah.lindqvist: Extension was granted to Sep 2026.
@dave.morton: thumbs up emoji
[Thread ends]
